# Slopwatch Implementation Workflow
# OpenProse workflow for implementing the dotnet-slopwatch tool

## Agents

agent researcher using sonnet
  skills: WebSearch, WebFetch, Read, Grep, Glob
  description: Researches code quality patterns, LLM reward hacking behaviors, and existing linter implementations

agent architect using opus
  skills: Read, Write, Edit, Grep, Glob
  description: Designs system architecture, interfaces, and project structure

agent implementer using sonnet
  skills: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob
  description: Implements C# code following the architecture design

agent tester using sonnet
  skills: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob
  description: Writes tests and creates test fixtures with intentional slop patterns

## Phase 1: Research

phase "Slop Pattern Research":
  researcher: Search for common LLM reward hacking patterns beyond the initial list (disabled tests, warning suppression, empty catch blocks, timeout jiggling). Look at slopometry, existing linters, and AI coding tool discussions.

  researcher: Document additional slop patterns to detect:
    - Magic number additions to make tests pass
    - Hardcoded expected values that match test assertions
    - Removing assertions from tests
    - Adding overly broad exception handlers
    - Commenting out problematic code instead of fixing it
    - Reducing test coverage by deleting tests
    - Adding retry loops to flaky tests
    - Loosening type constraints or validation

  researcher: Save findings to docs/slop-patterns.md

## Phase 2: Architecture

phase "Project Setup":
  architect: Create the solution structure:
    - src/Slopwatch/Slopwatch.csproj (core library, net9.0)
    - src/Slopwatch.Cmd/Slopwatch.Cmd.csproj (CLI tool)
    - tests/Slopwatch.Tests/Slopwatch.Tests.csproj (xUnit tests)
    - tests/Slopwatch.Tests.Fixtures/ (sloppy code samples)

  architect: Update Slopwatch.slnx with the new projects

  architect: Update Directory.Packages.props with dependencies:
    - LibGit2Sharp
    - Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.CSharp
    - CommandLineParser
    - xunit, xunit.runner.visualstudio
    - Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk
    - coverlet.collector

phase "Core Interfaces":
  architect: Design and create the core interfaces:
    - IDetectionRule with RuleId, Name, Description, Severity, AnalyzeAsync
    - DetectionContext with file info, syntax tree, changed lines
    - DetectionResult with location, message, suggested fix
    - DetectionSeverity enum (Info, Warning, Error)

## Phase 3: Implementation

phase "File Analysis":
  implementer: Implement FileAnalyzer for direct file analysis:
    - AnalyzeFile(path) to analyze a single file
    - AnalyzeFiles(paths) to analyze multiple files
    - AnalyzeDirectory(path, patterns) for bulk analysis

  implementer: Optionally implement GitDiffAnalyzer using libgit2sharp:
    - GetChangedFiles(targetBranch) for CI/CD branch comparison
    - This is secondary to direct file analysis

phase "Detection Rules":
  implementer: Implement DisabledTestRule (SW001):
    - Detect [Fact(Skip=...)], [Theory(Skip=...)]
    - Detect [Ignore], [IgnoreAttribute]
    - Detect #if false around test methods
    - Detect xUnit [Trait("Category", "Skip")] patterns

  implementer: Implement WarningSuppressRule (SW002):
    - Detect #pragma warning disable
    - Detect [SuppressMessage] attributes
    - Detect changes to .editorconfig severity levels
    - Detect NoWarn additions in .csproj files

  implementer: Implement EmptyCatchBlockRule (SW003):
    - Detect completely empty catch blocks
    - Detect catch blocks that only log without handling
    - Flag catch(Exception) without specific handling

  implementer: Implement TimeoutJigglingRule (SW004):
    - Detect Task.Delay in test files
    - Detect Thread.Sleep in test files
    - Detect SpinWait usage in tests

  loop until **all initially planned rules are implemented**:
    implementer: Implement next detection rule from the research findings

phase "CLI Tool":
  implementer: Implement Slopwatch.Cmd with CommandLineParser:
    - analyze command (default): run analysis
    - list-rules command: show available rules
    - init command: create config file

  implementer: Add CLI options:
    - --branch, -b: target branch to compare
    - --working-tree: analyze uncommitted changes
    - --output, -o: format (console, json, sarif)
    - --min-severity: filter threshold
    - --fail-on: exit code threshold
    - --config, -c: config file path

  implementer: Implement output formatters:
    - ConsoleOutputFormatter with colored output
    - JsonOutputFormatter for hook integration
    - SarifOutputFormatter for CI/CD integration

## Phase 4: Testing

phase "Test Fixtures":
  tester: Create test fixtures in Slopwatch.Tests.Fixtures/:
    - DisabledTestSamples.cs with various skip patterns
    - WarningSuppressSamples.cs with pragma and attributes
    - EmptyCatchSamples.cs with swallowed exceptions
    - TimeoutJigglingSamples.cs with delays in tests
    - CleanCodeSamples.cs with good patterns (should not trigger)

phase "Unit Tests":
  tester: Write unit tests for each detection rule:
    - Test positive detection (finds violations)
    - Test negative cases (clean code passes)
    - Test edge cases and variations

  tester: Write tests for DiffAnalyzer:
    - Mock git operations for unit tests
    - Test line change extraction

  loop until **all tests pass**:
    implementer: Fix failing tests
    tester: Verify fixes don't introduce regressions

phase "Integration Tests":
  tester: Create integration tests:
    - End-to-end CLI tests
    - Real git repository tests
    - Output format validation

## Phase 5: Integration

phase "CI/CD":
  implementer: Update .github/workflows/pr_validation.yml:
    - Build all projects
    - Run tests with coverage
    - Pack the tool

  implementer: Update .github/workflows/publish_nuget.yml:
    - Publish Slopwatch.Cmd as dotnet tool
    - Create GitHub release

phase "Hook Configuration":
  implementer: Create example hook configuration:
    - .claude/hooks/slopwatch.json for Claude Code
    - Document hook setup in README

phase "Documentation":
  implementer: Update README.md with:
    - Tool description and purpose
    - Installation instructions
    - Usage examples
    - Rule documentation
    - Hook integration guide

## Completion

phase "Verification":
  tester: Run full test suite
  tester: Verify CLI works end-to-end
  tester: Test hook integration manually

  loop until **the tool is production ready**:
    implementer: Address any remaining issues
    tester: Verify fixes

phase "Commit":
  implementer: Create commit with descriptive message
  implementer: Push to feature branch
  implementer: Create pull request with summary of changes
